{
    "_notes": [
        "Reconstructed Zaya Q4NX converter config (issue #1763).",
        "GGUF names follow the canonical llama.cpp ZAYA mapping (upstream PR #23112),",
        "mirrored in tools/convert_zaya_safetensors_to_gguf.py.",
        "Q4NX names match the manifest keys read by engine/npu/tools/zaya_cpu_runner.cpp.",
        "default_tensor_type=Q4_0 (signed symmetric, mins=0): the Zaya Q4NX packs",
        "value=(q-8)*scale (two's-complement nibble) with zero mins, per the research",
        "log (research/ws01-npu-attention/ZAYA-CCA-CPU-PORT.md session 9/13).",
        "CAVEAT: the actual zaya1-8b.q4nx was produced by tools/convert_float32_bins_to_q4nx.py",
        "(scale=abs_max/7, zp=0, ROW-major scales scales[row*8+group]). This GGUF converter's",
        "model_converter.py packs scales GROUP-major (group*32+row), so the scale byte order",
        "differs from that artifact; nibble/lane layout (parallel_size=16) matches."
    ],
    "q4nx_config": {
        "row_block_size": 32,
        "col_block_size": 256,
        "parallel_size": 16,
        "keep_block_in_2D": false
    },
